---
/**
 * Avatar with a perspective tilt that follows the pointer.
 *
 * This replaced a hand-drawn SVG line portrait. Dani's avatar is already a
 * 3D-style render, so using the real image gets the dimensional feel for
 * ~59 KB and a few lines of transform — where a real WebGL model would cost
 * ~150 KB gzipped of three.js plus an asset that could not actually be made
 * to resemble him.
 *
 * The image is plain <img> rather than astro:assets because that needs sharp,
 * and the file is already sized and compressed for its one display size.
 * Under prefers-reduced-motion the tilt is inert and it renders flat.
 */
---

<div class="avatar" data-avatar aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="avatar-inner">
    <img
      src="/img/avatar.jpg"
      alt=""
      width="420"
      height="746"
      decoding="async"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
  </div>
</div>
